FAQ = [
 ("What rear under-seat storage does my Silverado have?",
  "Lift the rear seat cushions. Crew Cab Silverados come with one of three setups: a carpeted floor with factory carpeted storage, a molded plastic storage box under the seat, or a plain floor with no storage. The listings on this page split along exactly those lines. 3W is cut for factory carpeted storage, Falafa and KUST for the rear under-seat storage box, and one budget set for trucks without the box. Husky's 94021 set is listed for trucks with carpet and underseat storage."),
 ("Do Silverado liners fit the GMC Sierra 1500?",
  "Yes, for the same cab and layout. The 2019+ Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 share the T1 cab, and most listings here name both trucks, including WeatherTech's front-bench set and Husky's 94021. Match the seat layout and rear storage version exactly as you would for a Silverado. Denali and AT4 interiors use the same floor pan."),
 ("Will 2019–2021 liners fit a 2022+ refreshed Silverado?",
  "The 2022 refresh changed the dashboard and, on most trims, moved the shifter to the console, but the floor pan carried over. WeatherTech's front-bench listing runs 2019–2026, KUST and 3W run 2019–2025, and LASFIT runs 2019–2026. The 'Silverado 1500 LTD' is the carryover 2022 model with the old interior, and several listings name it too."),
 ("Do I need a bench-seat or bucket-seat front liner?",
  "It depends on your front seats, and it matters on this truck because the front liner often wraps up the side of the console. LASFIT's set is listed for bucket seats only. WeatherTech sells separate part numbers for the front bench, and the budget set on this page is for a front bench without the rear storage box. Trucks with a front bench and a jump seat leave a center floor area that front-bench liners are cut to cover."),
 ("Are these liners compatible with Double Cab Silverados?",
  "No. Every set on this page is Crew Cab. The Double Cab has a shorter rear floor, and its rear liner is a different part. Husky's 13211 front pair lists Double and Crew Cab, so you can share the front row, but buy a Double Cab rear liner separately. Count your doors: Double Cab rear doors are shorter than the front ones."),
 ("Is WeatherTech worth the extra money on a Silverado?",
  "If you want a laser-measured liner from a brand that publishes where it's made and a lifetime limited warranty, yes. WeatherTech says its liners are laser-measured and backed by a lifetime limited warranty, and its FloorLiner HP line is injection-molded TPE made in America. Budget TPE sets fit well too, but their makers publish less. On a truck you plan to keep, the warranty is the main difference you can verify."),
 ("Will a liner fit around the rear under-seat storage box lid?",
  "Only if it's cut for the box. The plastic storage box changes the rear floor profile, so a liner cut for a flat or carpeted floor either won't sit flat or will block the box. Falafa and KUST list their sets for trucks with the box. If you're unsure, photograph your rear floor and send it to the seller before ordering."),
 ("How do I stop a liner from sliding under the pedals?",
  "Remove the factory carpet mat, set the liner directly on the carpet and lock it onto the driver-side retention posts. Every listing here claims a Silverado-specific cut, which includes the post holes. Push the liner forward with your heel after installing; if it moves, it isn't seated. Never stack a liner on top of another mat."),
 ("How do I clean TPE liners in winter?",
  "Pull them out, knock the slush off, rinse with warm water and a little dish soap, and let them dry. Avoid silicone protectants or tire shine, which make the surface slick. Empty them every few days in salt season so the melted slush doesn't overflow the walls onto the carpet."),
]

